@claude explain the PP numerics change with easy-to-understand examples before vs. after

> 1F1B goes from 5 to 3 reduce-scatters per step

sounds that we should do it?

@claude 

What still puzzles me is "reduce-scatter mb0" on F0. My impression has been that, without chunked loss wrapper, every FSDP module will only incur one reduce-scatter across all the PP microbatches, after the last backward happens. Correct me if I'm wrong.

It seems it's not the case with chunked loss wrapper, even with changes in this PR. Regardless of whether or not we fix in this PR (I think we should), is there a way that we defer this mb0 reduce-scatter on lm_head as well?
